  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The two shorter sides of a right-angled triangle have length $7+2\\sqrt{3}$ and $7-2\\sqrt{3}$.\n\nFind:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the length of the hypotenuse of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{122}$",
          "worked": "Let $h$ be the hypotenuse. By Pythagoras’ theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=(7+2\\sqrt{3})^2+(7-2\\sqrt{3})^2\\\\h^2&=49+28\\sqrt{3}+12+49-28\\sqrt{3}+12\\\\h^2&=122\\\\h&=\\sqrt{122}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the perimeter of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$14+\\sqrt{122}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=(7+2\\sqrt{3})+(7-2\\sqrt{3})+\\sqrt{122}\\\\P&=14+\\sqrt{122}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the area of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{37}{2}$",
          "worked": "The two shorter sides are perpendicular, so they provide the base and height.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(7+2\\sqrt{3})(7-2\\sqrt{3})\\\\A&=\\frac12\\left(7^2-(2\\sqrt{3})^2\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac12(49-12)\\\\A&=\\frac{37}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
